balance deterrence and diplomacy during its escalating conflict with the Iran-backed Houthis in neighboring Yemen.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why the era of cheap government debt is over</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e3db92e5d170c5310cc55eff8289c61fc3ec17d59b49f5525900a958e23a2a0</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272--435550125c87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US debt has topped $40 trillion. How risky is the country's growing debt burden. And will investors keep funding Washington's deficits?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>US allies in Asia alarmed as think tank calls for pullback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6fb5bddfa1bb3e90fd026a5fd15399a5b95d6b2842bf68531fafd1ebd88f651f</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554--5c1e9b8e70e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Analysts warn that a US withdrawal from the western Pacific, as recently suggested by a think tank, would weaken deterrence and strengthen China's position.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>'Woman, Life, Freedom' spirit lives on as Iran war drags on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c41da6141bc1e47f299b7eac309999e7e4e90e776a20cc3fae5b6e1ac85f2346</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:45:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/woman-life-freedom-spirit-lives-on-as-iran-war-drags-on/a-79276123--90098f2ae3f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/woman-life-freedom-spirit-lives-on-as-iran-war-drags-on/a-79276123?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2022 death of Jina Mahsa Amini in police custody triggered a resistance movement in Iran. Four years later, the Iranian regime endures — but so does the legacy of the "Woman, Life, Freedom" protests.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Netherlands: Suspected sabotage disrupts train services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9af242a9efebbb0a022e8c51d7b916f12e3ae0e5096b5f02009f9a7528e5aa04</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600--a0c80c1ea5f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A major outage has hit parts of the Dutch railway system after objects were found placed across lines, authorities say. The company responsible for rail infrastructure says it suspects deliberate wrongdoing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Europe launches two climate observation satellites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e4331f64a2d48cd870bb118f35ea9df850096acc54dc9953759edf12004f3dd</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705--7858649e62ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Space Agency has put two satellites into orbit to take a closer look at the impact of climate change. One of them will focus particularly on plant life.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU seeks Arctic strategy amid growing power rivalry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a531a321f72d166a54c67270a49c2462969604dbefe5286f05eccb5e8062ef6</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-arctic-strategy-amid-growing-power-rivalry/a-79266739--8da58b1eb0cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-arctic-strategy-amid-growing-power-rivalry/a-79266739?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's aggression, Trump's threats against Greenland and the race for critical raw materials are pushing the Arctic to the top of Europe's agenda.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, Russia set for new round of US-mediated talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:558642264533e8e7637ef2579523201bd4f13a3ac164b4cdc99d67e272c03417</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T18:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-set-for-new-round-of-us-mediated-talks/a-79261147--0cf6c10eaa61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-set-for-new-round-of-us-mediated-talks/a-79261147?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New trilateral talks between Ukraine, Russia and the US could begin in October, according to Kyiv and Moscow. Few expect a breakthrough, but Ukraine is seeking a partial de-escalation to help it get through the winter.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trump seeks halt to energy attacks by both Russia, Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:375de68caa789de33bf1ca5961fdf0b1dd314bb05840b03a8293aedc9677d272</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T17:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-seeks-halt-to-energy-attacks-by-both-russia-ukraine/a-79265774--121a884cf5a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-seeks-halt-to-energy-attacks-by-both-russia-ukraine/a-79265774?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump, under fire for record US diesel prices, claims Russia and Ukraine have agreed to stop striking energy targets. Russia said nothing; Ukraine said "we expect specifics from our partners" on any such move.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's richest man Dangote's IPO out of reach in Nigeria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9dfd98f27c3f6c3b900d01736063c6875f69cd3113ab7a7ed43fcb33e1a8792</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-richest-man-dangote-s-ipo-out-of-reach-in-nigeria/a-79263398--03e0d1756308.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-richest-man-dangote-s-ipo-out-of-reach-in-nigeria/a-79263398?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dangote seeks $1.6 billion from investors to finance a $14.3 billion expansion and thus double the oil refinery's capacity. The offer could give millions of Nigerians a stake in the company. But who can truly afford it?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
